    <section id="cover" class="cover">
      <div class="brand">DMTSP · Consumer Industry Practice</div>
      <div class="title">Sellers <span class="accent">Handbook</span></div>
      <div class="subtitle">to Agentic AI on Microsoft</div>
      <div class="volume-badge">Cliff Notes Edition</div>
      <div class="edition">Companion to the APEX-M Trilogy · v1.0 · 2026-05-12</div>
      <p class="tagline">
        A scan-and-go handbook for sellers who need to attach Deloitte's
        Agentic AI Delivery Services to a Deloitte practice — one
        Microsoft growth platform at a time, from a Power BI wedge to a
        B2C transformation.
      </p>
      <div class="wrox-label">Practice-Ready · One Page Per Idea</div>
      <div class="byline">Keven Markham · Vice President, DMTSP</div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== HOW TO USE =========== -->
    <section id="how-to-use" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Front Matter</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">How to Use This Handbook</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Audience</td><td>Deloitte sellers attaching DMTSP services to an industry practice.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Read time</td><td>60 seconds per chapter. The whole book in under an hour.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Posture</td><td>You are <em>not</em> selling APEX to clients. You are attaching <em>Agentic AI Delivery Services</em> to a practice, using APEX as Deloitte's internal accelerator.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output</td><td>Every chapter ends with one move you can make tomorrow.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>Each chapter is one page of Cliff Notes. The pattern repeats so you
      can flip to any chapter cold and get value in 60 seconds:</p>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>At a Glance</strong> — the four facts that matter.</li>
        <li><strong>Seller Steps</strong> — the numbered ladder for that move.</li>
        <li><strong>Say / Don't Say</strong> — the language test.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Attach</strong> — which growth platform pulls in.</li>
        <li><strong>Independence Guardrail</strong> — the SEC/PCAOB test.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Reminder</div>
        Deloitte audits Microsoft. The commercial structure must stay clean
        at every level: <strong>platform from Microsoft, services from
        Deloitte, two separate contracts.</strong> APEX is internal IP
        and never appears on a client SOW.
      </div>
    </section>

