      <h3>The Four Unlock Steps — what the seller actually says</h3>
      <div class="step-grid">
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">U1</span><span class="step-body"><strong>L0 → L1</strong> · the cold open. "I'll build you a Power BI Opportunity Heatmap for your portfolio. Five days. Free. You own the .pbix."</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">U2</span><span class="step-body"><strong>L1 → L2</strong> · the wedge unlock. "Now you can see every place APEX would compress your delivery — want to act on the top three?"</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">U3</span><span class="step-body"><strong>L2 → L3</strong> · the Wave-1-proved unlock. "Wave 1 returned X in 90 days against Y of services spend. Want to scale this pattern across the practice?"</span></div>
        <div class="step"><span class="step-num">U4</span><span class="step-body"><strong>L3 → L4</strong> · the consumer unlock. "Your B2B is humming. When do we go to your clients' consumers?"</span></div>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top:14px;">
        <span class="src ms">Microsoft</span>
        <span class="src deloitte">Deloitte</span>
        <span class="src apex">APEX</span>
        <span class="src practice">Practice</span>
        Four component classes appear in the diagram. Microsoft = the platform the client licenses directly. Deloitte = the services that close the SOW. APEX = the internal delivery accelerator that compresses 18 months to 9. Practice = the buyer that opens the door.
      </p>

      <h3>The Seller Journey — Six Phases, End to End</h3>
      <p>Every chapter with Seller Steps lives in one of six phases. The
      Carry-Forward block at the end of each chapter names exactly what
      flows in (Inputs), what the chapter produces (Outputs), and which
      chapter is next. Follow the chain from <strong>Ready</strong> to
      <strong>Annuity</strong> and the seller motion runs itself.</p>

      <div class="journey-strip">
        <div class="js-phase ready">
          <span class="js-num">1</span>
          <span class="js-name">Ready</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 1 · 2 · 3 · 12</div>
        </div>
        <div class="js-phase meet">
          <span class="js-num">2</span>
          <span class="js-name">Meet</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 4 · 5 · 23</div>
        </div>
        <div class="js-phase wedge">
          <span class="js-num">3</span>
          <span class="js-name">Wedge</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 19 · L1</div>
        </div>
        <div class="js-phase sell">
          <span class="js-num">4</span>
          <span class="js-name">Sell</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 20 · 25 · L2 + BVA</div>
        </div>
        <div class="js-phase scale">
          <span class="js-num">5</span>
          <span class="js-name">Scale</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 21 · L3</div>
        </div>
        <div class="js-phase annuity">
          <span class="js-num">6</span>
          <span class="js-name">Annuity</span>
          <div class="js-chapters">Ch 22 · L4</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:13.5px;color:var(--dim);margin-top:12px;">
        <strong>Cross-cutting advisory references:</strong> the six Microsoft
        Growth Platform chapters (Ch 6 Fabric · Ch 7 Foundry · Ch 8 Copilot ·
        Ch 9 Purview · Ch 10 Entra · Ch 11 D365) are pulled into the journey
        wherever the platform attach motion fires — typically during the
        Sell and Scale phases.
      </p>

      <h3>Revenue Influence — One Practice, Four Levels</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Action</th><th>Revenue Type</th><th>Potential</th><th>Microsoft Growth Platforms</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>L1</td><td>Power BI Opportunity Heatmap</td><td>Wedge</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$25–75K</span></td><td><span class="ms-chip">Power BI</span> <span class="ms-chip">Fabric</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>L2</td><td>First Wave 1 agent deployment</td><td>New</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$500K–$2M</span></td><td><span class="ms-chip">Fabric</span> <span class="ms-chip">Foundry</span> <span class="ms-chip">Copilot</span> <span class="ms-chip">Purview</span> <span class="ms-chip">Entra</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>L3</td><td>Practice CoE + B2B fleet</td><td>Expansion</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$5–20M</span></td><td>+ <span class="ms-chip">Logic Apps</span> <span class="ms-chip">Azure AI Agent Svc</span> <span class="ms-chip">MCP</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>L4</td><td>B2C consumer agentic</td><td>Strategic / Displacement</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$20–50M+</span></td><td>+ <span class="ms-chip">Dynamics 365</span> <span class="ms-chip">M365 Copilot</span> <span class="ms-chip">D365 Customer Insights</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
