    <!-- ===== CH 1 ===== -->
    <section id="ch1" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">What You Sell</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>You sell</td><td>Deloitte Agentic AI Delivery Services (advisory · implement · operate).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Client buys</td><td>Microsoft platform licenses <em>direct</em> from Microsoft.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>APEX is</td><td>Deloitte's internal delivery accelerator. Never on a client SOW.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Why it matters</td><td>Deloitte audits Microsoft. Clean separation is non-negotiable.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Lead with the service, not the tool.</strong> Open every conversation with "Deloitte's Agentic AI Delivery Services."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Memorize the one-line opener verbatim</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Review the service catalog (advisory · implement · operate · sustain)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Practice not saying "APEX" in the first 5 minutes</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pre-write the closing sentence: "Two contracts, one program"</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Name the platform second.</strong> "On your Microsoft platform — Fabric, Foundry, Copilot."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the client's existing Microsoft footprint before the meeting</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map their entitlements: EA · MCA-E · which Copilot SKUs</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify the Microsoft seller for joint motions</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Never imply Deloitte resells Microsoft</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Reference APEX only internally.</strong> "Our delivery accelerator compresses 18 months to 9."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Use "delivery accelerator" externally; "APEX" only internally</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Slides redacted — APEX never appears on a client deck</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Have the 18→9 compression evidence ready (Wave 1 reference)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Talk about <em>outcomes</em>, not methodology</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Never quote APEX as a SKU.</strong> No "$X per user/month." Ever.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>SOW is priced as a service engagement (Wave / fixed-fee / T&amp;M)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No per-seat, per-agent, or per-call APEX line item</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft consumption is the client's invoice, not Deloitte's</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Independence review before any pricing leaves the room</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip ready">Phase 1 · Ready</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 1 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">The <a href="#sellers-dream">Sellers Dream</a> diagram · the three-way relationship truth (Client × Microsoft × Deloitte)</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Memorized opener · APEX-as-accelerator framing · SKU-free pricing posture</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch2">Ch 2 · The Two-Contract Rule</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="saynot">
        <div class="col say">
          <h4>✓ Say</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>"Deloitte delivers your agentic program on your Microsoft platform."</li>
            <li>"We use proprietary accelerators to deploy in months, not years."</li>
            <li>"Two contracts: services from Deloitte, platform from Microsoft."</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col nope">
          <h4>✗ Don't Say</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>"Buy APEX."</li>
            <li>"APEX is Deloitte's product."</li>
            <li>"APEX comes with Microsoft."</li>
            <li>"We'll give you an APEX license."</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Guardrail</div>
        If a regulator read your slide, would they conclude Deloitte and
        Microsoft have a commingled commercial offering? The answer must
        always be <strong>no</strong>.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 2 ===== -->
    <section id="ch2" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The Two-Contract Rule</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Contract A</td><td>Client ↔ Microsoft. Platform licensing. EA, MCA-E, or pay-as-you-go.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Contract B</td><td>Client ↔ Deloitte. Services SOW under MSA.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Never</td><td>Resell, bundle, or pass-through Microsoft licensing through Deloitte.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Co-fund OK</td><td>Microsoft MCI, ECIF, and partner-of-record motions, properly disclosed.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Open the conversation with two pieces of paper.</strong> Draw the two contracts on a whiteboard. Make the boundary visible.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Box 1: Client ↔ Microsoft (platform licensing)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Box 2: Client ↔ Deloitte (services SOW under MSA)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Draw the boundary line — no connecting arrow between them</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Annotate "two invoices, one program" underneath</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Confirm the Microsoft side is procured.</strong> If not, name the Microsoft seller who will close it; do not promise to close it for them.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Check the client's EA / MCA-E status</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify the Microsoft AE / ATU lead by name</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the Fabric / Foundry / Copilot SKUs in flight</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Introduce the Microsoft seller to the client — do not represent them</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Scope your SOW around outcomes.</strong> Wave 1 ROI, agent count, HITL gate maturity — not Microsoft consumption.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Outcomes section: ROI target + agent count + gate maturity</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No Microsoft consumption commitments inside the SOW</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Acceptance criteria tied to Wave 1 audit-row evidence</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Independence reviewer named on the SOW cover</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Add a co-fund line if applicable.</strong> Microsoft Cloud Investment (MCI), ECIF, or partner-of-record — disclose, do not hide.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft co-fund instrument identified (MCI · ECIF · POR)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Disclose the co-fund alongside the SOW — never inside it</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft signs the co-fund letter, not Deloitte</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Independence reviewer confirms structure</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Sign Contract B independently.</strong> Deloitte's SOW stands on its own value, even if MCI never lands.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Deloitte SOW has independent business case</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No contingency clauses on Microsoft co-fund</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Wave 1 ROI defensible without co-fund</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Client signs Deloitte SOW even if Microsoft motion is delayed</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip ready">Phase 1 · Ready</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 2 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 1 language discipline · client Microsoft footprint (EA / MCA-E)</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Two-box whiteboard diagram · Microsoft seller named · Independence review pathway</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch3">Ch 3 · Who You Sell To</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <div class="callout-label">Trap</div>
        Sellers who promise Microsoft credits inside a Deloitte SOW create
        an Independence breach. Co-fund is a Microsoft motion that travels
        <em>alongside</em> Deloitte's contract, never <em>inside</em> it.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 3 ===== -->
    <section id="ch3" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Who You Sell To</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Primary buyer</td><td>A Deloitte <strong>industry practice</strong> (RC, TH, HLS, ER, TMT, ICE).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Secondary buyer</td><td>The practice's <strong>LCSP / PPMD / Engagement Partner</strong> for a named account.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Internal buy first</td><td>Practice leaders are gatekeepers to their client portfolios.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Client buyer (eventual)</td><td>Client CIO, CDO, CFO — but only after the practice opens the door.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pick one practice.</strong> Start with the one whose APEX edition is most mature — Retail & Consumer (RC) ships today.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Cross-reference edition status (RC / TH = active today)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the practice has 10+ named accounts in scope</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Check the GSSC Lab is provisioned for that edition</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Lock the target practice by name in the seller plan</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Map the leadership.</strong> Identify the Industry Leader, the Tech Leader, and the top 3 LCSPs by revenue.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pull the practice org chart</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Name the Industry Leader (typical buyer for L3+)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Name the Tech Leader (typical first wedge entry)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Rank the top 3 LCSPs by bookings; note their portfolios</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Approach the Tech Leader first.</strong> They have least to lose by trying APEX-accelerated services.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Cold-outreach email or warm intro through DMTSP</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>30-min slot · discovery only · no deck</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Reference any prior agent pilots in the practice</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Offer the L1 wedge as the gift at the close of the meeting</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Use the L1 wedge.</strong> Offer the Power BI Dashboard before asking for anything.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No SOW conversation in the wedge meeting</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Free dashboard offer · 5 working days</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Practice owns the .pbix on handover</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Schedule the data pull before leaving the room</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Earn the LCSP introduction.</strong> The Tech Leader brings you to the LCSP after the dashboard lands.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Deliver L1 on time · 5 days · no scope creep</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Walk the Tech Leader through the heatmap output</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Ask: "which LCSP should see this first?"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Tech Leader makes the warm intro — you do not cold-call</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip ready">Phase 1 · Ready</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 3 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 1 + Ch 2 · APEX edition status (RC / TH = active today)</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Target practice locked · Tech Leader named · top 3 LCSPs ranked · practice account list</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch-fa-discover">Ch 12 · Discovery Framework</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">Key Play</div>
        Practices that already attach Microsoft licensing growth to their
        accounts are pre-qualified. Ask the Microsoft account team which
        Deloitte practices are net-new MCI consumers — that is your
        target list.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== PART II — THE GSSC LAB =========== -->
    <section class="part-opener" id="part-gccs">
      <div class="part-label">Part II</div>
      <h1 class="part-title">The GSSC Lab — Pre-Built Accelerator</h1>
      <p class="part-intro">
        Before you sell any platform or any service, know what is already
        running. The GSSC Lab is Deloitte's pre-built, Microsoft-native
        delivery environment — platform stood up, Agent 365 wired,
        Scenario Matcher live, per-practice service bundles registered.
        Two chapters: what's pre-built, and how Agent 365 + Scenario
        Matcher + Practice Services interlock to compress your sales
        cycle from quarters to weeks.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 4 — GSSC LAB OVERVIEW ===== -->
    <section id="ch-gccs" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The GSSC Lab — Pre-Built for Quick Turnaround</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Deloitte's <strong>GSSC Lab</strong> — a fully provisioned Microsoft-native environment with APEX, Agent 365, and per-practice service bundles ready to demo.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Why it matters</td><td>Skip 6–8 weeks of environment build. Demo on Day 1. Wave 1 pilot in <strong>30 days</strong>, not 90.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Who owns it</td><td>DMTSP Consumer Industry team. Bookable by any Deloitte practice.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Where it lives</td><td>Deloitte tenant. Synthetic data only. Independence-clean.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>What's Already Running</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
