              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft SKU sizing aligned with Lab usage profile</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Wave 1 kickoff date scheduled in client tenant</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip meet">Phase 2 · Meet</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 5 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 3 target practice · Ch 12 scenario shortlist · 3 target accounts named</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">GSSC Lab slot booked · Scenario Matcher pre-loaded with account context</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch-agent365">Ch 5 · Agent 365 · Matcher live demo</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="saynot">
        <div class="col say">
          <h4>✓ Say</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>"This is Deloitte's lab — pre-built, working today."</li>
            <li>"We promote from here into your tenant for production."</li>
            <li>"You're looking at Agent 365 running an APEX edition agent."</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col nope">
          <h4>✗ Don't Say</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>"This is your environment." (it's Deloitte's)</li>
            <li>"This is what you'll license." (services, not platform)</li>
            <li>"Microsoft built this for us." (Independence breach)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        The Lab is where the platform attach motion <em>starts</em>. Every
        demo is a live environment the client will eventually buy capacity
        for — Fabric, Foundry, Agent 365, Copilot, Purview. The seller
        models the SKU mix in the Lab and shows the client what their
        version costs.
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Guardrail</div>
        The Lab runs on Deloitte tenant with synthetic data. No client
        data ever enters the GSSC Lab. Promotion to client tenant is an
        L2 motion under the client's separate Microsoft licensing.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 5 — AGENT 365 + MATCHER + SERVICES ===== -->
    <section id="ch-agent365" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Agent 365 · Scenario Matcher · Practice Services</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Agent 365</td><td>Microsoft's agent framework. Native runtime for production agents across Teams, Copilot, Foundry, M365.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scenario Matcher</td><td>APEX-built decision engine. Maps practice + account + pain → top 3 scenarios + ROI + Microsoft SKU list.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice Services</td><td>Per-edition bundles of advisory · implement · operate. Pre-priced, pre-staffed, pre-templated.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How they interlock</td><td>Matcher picks the scenario · Agent 365 runs the agent · Practice Services ships the SOW.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Component 1 · Microsoft Agent 365 (the Framework)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Production runtime</strong> for agents — hosted, governed, audited natively.</li>
        <li><strong>Surfaces:</strong> Teams · Outlook · Copilot Studio · M365 apps · custom web.</li>
        <li><strong>Native HITL gates</strong>, audit rows, Entra identity binding — APEX gate taxonomy plugs in directly.</li>
        <li><strong>APEX edition agents</strong> deploy onto Agent 365 as the runtime substrate. No bespoke runtime to build.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Component 2 · APEX Scenario Matcher (the Decision Engine)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Input:</strong> practice (RC, TH, HLS…) + account profile + industry + top pain.</li>
        <li><strong>Output:</strong> top 3 APEX scenarios · estimated Wave 1 ROI · Microsoft attach SKU list · matching Practice Service bundle.</li>
        <li><strong>Where it runs:</strong> in the GSSC Lab, on top of Foundry. Live, interactive, demo-ready.</li>
        <li><strong>When you use it:</strong> during the 10-minute conversation. Leader watches their accounts come back with matched plays in seconds.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Component 3 · Practice Service Bundles (the SOW Builder)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>One bundle per edition × phase</strong> — Discover, Design, Build, Deploy, Operate.</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-priced</strong> — no waiting on a pricing committee for a first SOW.</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-staffed</strong> — the Lab knows which Deloitte FTEs are available per practice.</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-templated</strong> — SOW skeleton, BVA baseline, MSA references all populated.</li>
        <li><strong>Sellers configure, not author.</strong> Pick from the menu; tune for the account.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Seller Steps — Using All Three Live</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Open the Scenario Matcher</strong> on the tablet during the practice conversation.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Scenario Matcher pre-warmed in the GSSC Lab</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Tablet on the table, screen visible to the leader</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Mirror to room display if available</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Practice edition pre-selected (RC · TH · …)</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Drop in the 3 target accounts.</strong> One row each: name · industry · top pain.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Type each account name live — the leader sees you working</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm industry tag per account</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Capture top pain in the leader's own words</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Click "Match" — let the leader see the spinner</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Read the matched scenarios aloud.</strong> Practice leader sees their own portfolio come back with plays.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Read top 3 scenarios for each account</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Surface ROI confidence + Microsoft attach SKUs</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Note which scenario the leader reacts to most</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Anchor the conversation on the top-ranked scenario</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Click the top scenario</strong> to launch the live Agent 365 demo. Real agent, real audit row, real seconds.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Live agent runs in Foundry · seconds, not minutes</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>HITL gate shown in action</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Audit row written to Purview — point at the row</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft consumption profile visible (Fabric · Foundry)</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Display the matching Practice Service Bundle.</strong> Show price, duration, staffing.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pull the per-edition Wave 1 bundle</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Show price range · duration · staffing</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Reference Microsoft attach SKUs from earlier</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the bundle is on the Practice Service Catalog</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Hand them the bundle name on a sticky note.</strong> That is the shape of the L2 SOW.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Write bundle name + Wave 1 timeline + ROI range</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Hand the sticky to the practice leader directly</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm next step + named owner before leaving</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Log the bundle + sticky text in the opportunity tracker</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Promise the .pbix dashboard</strong> as the L1 wedge. Schedule kickoff before you leave.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>L1 commitment: 5 working days, free, .pbix handover</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Name the practice contact for the data pull</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Lock the kickoff date in the leader's calendar</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Send confirmation email same-day</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip meet">Phase 2 · Meet</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 6 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 4 Lab slot + accounts loaded · Ch 12 discovery card · practice leader in the room</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Matched scenarios surfaced live · sticky note bundle handed over · L1 commitment scheduled</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch14">Ch 23 · The 10-Minute Practice Conversation</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Practice Service Bundles — At a Glance</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Practice</th><th>Edition</th><th>Wave 1 Bundle</th><th>Indicative Range</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Retail · Consumer Goods</td><td>RC</td><td>Demand-forecast or assortment agent, 90 days</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$750K–$1.5M</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hospitality · Aviation · Travel</td><td>TH</td><td>Yield-management or guest-experience agent</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$750K–$1.5M</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Health Care · Life Sciences</td><td>HLS</td><td>Prior-auth or supply-chain agent <em>(planned)</em></td><td><span class="rev-chip">$900K–$2M</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>TMT</td><td>TMT</td><td>Network ops or content-rights agent <em>(planned)</em></td><td><span class="rev-chip">$800K–$1.8M</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Energy · Resources</td><td>ER</td><td>Asset-integrity or trading agent <em>(planned)</em></td><td><span class="rev-chip">$1M–$2.5M</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Automotive · Heavy Equip</td><td>ICE</td><td>Aftermarket or warranty agent <em>(planned)</em></td><td><span class="rev-chip">$900K–$2M</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        Agent 365 is Microsoft's production agent runtime. Every Wave 1
        deployment is an Agent 365 consumption commitment. Selling
        APEX-on-Agent-365 is selling Microsoft platform growth — and the
        client's Microsoft seller sees the attach.
      </div>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">Key Play</div>
        Walk the practice leader through their <em>own</em> three accounts
        in the Scenario Matcher live. The moment they see their portfolio
        return matched scenarios and a bundle price, the L2 conversation
        is already underway. No deck moves this fast.
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Guardrail</div>
        Matcher outputs are Deloitte service recommendations. Microsoft
        SKU list is for sizing only — the client procures Microsoft
        licensing directly under their own EA/MCA-E. Two contracts,
        always.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== PART III — MICROSOFT GROWTH PLATFORMS =========== -->
    <section class="part-opener" id="part2">
      <div class="part-label">Part III</div>
      <h1 class="part-title">The Six Microsoft Growth Platforms</h1>
      <p class="part-intro">
        Every level of the ladder attaches a different combination of
        Microsoft growth platforms. These six chapters are your platform
        Cliff Notes — what each one is, when to lead with it, and what
        the practice actually cares about. The Lab in Part II is where
        you demo these live; this part is how you talk about them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 4 — FABRIC ===== -->
    <section id="ch4" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 6 · Growth Platform 1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Fabric — the Data Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Unified data platform. OneLake, Direct Lake, Real-Time Intelligence, Data Factory.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Practice's clients have 3+ data silos and no system of record for agents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>Wave 1 cannot start without an SoR. Fabric is the cheapest path to one.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>Every level.</strong> Fabric is the foundation. Power BI runs on it (L1).</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Ask "where does the agent get its truth?"</strong> If the answer is more than one system, lead with Fabric.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Inventory the client's source systems for the use case</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map current SoR fragmentation (how many systems?)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify the "single truth" gap for the target agent</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Anchor the conversation: agent needs one SoR, not seven</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Position OneLake as the SoR.</strong> Bronze · Silver · Gold medallion — APEX defaults to Direct Lake on Gold.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Draw the medallion diagram (Bronze → Silver → Gold)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Show Direct Lake reading from Gold without copy</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Reference APEX's default Direct Lake binding</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm OneLake shortcuts cover the existing data planes</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire Power BI on top.</strong> L1 wedge becomes the proof point — same lakehouse will feed L2 agents.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>L1 dashboard runs on the same Gold lakehouse as future agents</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Show the lakehouse → Power BI → Foundry continuity</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>L1 data model becomes the L2 semantic model</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No throw-away work between L1 and L2</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Attach Fabric capacity to the SOW.</strong> Client buys capacity from Microsoft; Deloitte models the right F-SKU.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Model the F-SKU for Wave 1 workload (F64+ floor)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Client procures capacity from Microsoft directly</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No Fabric line item inside the Deloitte SOW</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft seller introduced for the capacity motion</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · pulled into Wave 1 design (Ch 20)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch-fa-discover">Ch 12</a> use case · <a href="#ch11">Ch 20</a> Wave 1 scope · client source-system inventory</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Fabric F-SKU sizing model · OneLake medallion plan · capacity attach path (client-direct)</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next ref →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch5">Ch 7 · Foundry — the Agent Plane</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        Fabric F64+ is the practical floor for agentic workloads. Smaller
        SKUs throttle Direct Lake. Position F64 as the Wave 1 baseline.
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Note</div>
        Fabric capacity is licensed by the client. Deloitte models it,
        sizes it, and deploys against it — but the capacity invoice is
        from Microsoft.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 5 — FOUNDRY ===== -->
    <section id="ch5" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 7 · Growth Platform 2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Azure AI Foundry — the Agent Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Model catalog, agent runtime, evaluation, observability for production agents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Client is past PoC and needs governed, repeatable agent deployment.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>Agent fleet management. APEX edition catalogs (30–34 agents) deploy here.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>L2 onward.</strong> First agent goes here.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pull the edition agent catalog.</strong> RC has 34 agents pre-mapped to Foundry projects.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Open APEX edition registry for the practice</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map each agent to a Foundry project / connection</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Note pre-built MCP tool bindings per agent</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify "shipping today" vs. "synthetic only" agents</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pick one Wave 1 agent.</strong> Highest-blast-radius, lowest-PII. Demand-forecast or assortment, typically.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Score top 3 candidates on blast radius × PII risk</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm scenario has clean data lineage</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Validate ROI via BVA before locking the choice</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Engagement Partner signs off on Wave 1 selection</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire HITL gate.</strong> APEX Core Part 8.3 — HITL / ACK_ONLY / ZERO_TOUCH / ESCALATION. Foundry holds the gate state.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pick gate type per decision class</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Define approver roles for HITL escalation</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Wire gate state to Foundry agent definition</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Test gate path end-to-end before production</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Bind audit rows.</strong> Every agent decision writes an audit row to Fabric. APEX provides the schema.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Install APEX audit-row schema in Gold</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Foundry agent writes per-decision row</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Purview captures audit row in lineage</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>30-day audit-row count baseline established</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · pulled into Wave 1 design (Ch 20)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch4">Ch 6 Fabric</a> SoR · <a href="#ch-fa-discover">Ch 12</a> scenario · APEX edition agent catalog</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Wave 1 agent selected · HITL gate type · audit-row schema installed in Foundry workspace</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next ref →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch6">Ch 8 · Copilot — the Experience Plane</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        Foundry consumption pulls Fabric (state) and Copilot (UX) along
        with it. The three platforms attach as a triad.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 6 — COPILOT ===== -->
    <section id="ch6" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 8 · Growth Platform 3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Microsoft 365 Copilot — the Experience Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Conversational surface in Teams, Outlook, Word, Excel. Copilot Studio for custom agents.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Client wants frontline users to <em>talk</em> to APEX agents, not log into a tool.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>Adoption. Users already live in Teams. No new login.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>L2–L3.</strong> Becomes the surface for internal B2B agents.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Confirm M365 E3/E5 + Copilot SKU.</strong> Without the Copilot SKU, Studio agents can't ride in Teams.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Check client M365 tenant SKU mix (E3 / E5)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm Copilot SKU coverage for target persona</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>If missing, scope the Copilot SKU motion with Microsoft seller</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pilot user count modeled in Wave 1 plan</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pick the persona.</strong> Store-101 facilitator, GM, regional buyer — APEX has reference personas per edition.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pull APEX reference personas for the practice edition</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map persona to a real role in the client org</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm 20–50 named users for pilot cohort</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Recruit persona champion for change-mgmt</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire Copilot Studio agent.</strong> Studio agent calls APEX Foundry agent. Studio is the surface; Foundry is the brain.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Build Studio agent skin per persona</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Wire Studio agent → Foundry call via typed contract</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pin agent to Teams sidebar for pilot users</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>End-to-end test from Teams click → Foundry → audit row</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Measure adoption weekly.</strong> Active-user count is the Wave 1 success metric, alongside ROI.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Weekly active user (WAU) dashboard live</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Decision velocity tracked alongside WAU</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>WAU plateau triggers persona-tuning review</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Adoption number in every QBR with the client</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · pulled into Wave 1 design (Ch 20)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch5">Ch 7</a> agent picked · M365 SKU mix · APEX reference personas</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Persona-to-role mapping · Copilot SKU coverage · Studio surface designed · WAU dashboard live</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next ref →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch7">Ch 9 · Purview — the Trust Plane</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">Key Play</div>
        "Your users already know Teams. Their agents will live there too."
        This sentence closes more L2 deals than any ROI slide.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 7 — PURVIEW ===== -->
    <section id="ch7" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 9 · Growth Platform 4</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Microsoft Purview — the Trust Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Data governance, sensitivity labels, DLP, audit, compliance — across Fabric/Foundry/Copilot.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Client legal, risk, or audit asks "where does our data go?" before signing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>Unblocks the deal. Purview is the answer to half the procurement questions.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>L2 onward.</strong> Required before any agent touches PII.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Run the data-classification scan early.</strong> Purview maps sensitivity before agents are built.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Purview scan scoped to Wave 1 data planes</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Sensitivity labels applied to PII / PHI / financial</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>DLP policies authored per label class</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Scan results reviewed with client privacy team</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire Purview labels to APEX HITL gates.</strong> Sensitive data = HITL required. APEX enforces by label.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map each label to a gate class (HITL · ACK · ZERO_TOUCH)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Foundry agent reads label at runtime</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Gate routing test for each label class</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Privacy lead signs off on the label → gate matrix</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Attach to procurement.</strong> Hand the client a Purview-grounded data-flow diagram. Lawyers sign faster.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Generate Purview-backed data-flow diagram for the use case</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Annotate every data egress point and its label</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Walk procurement / legal through the diagram</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Use the diagram as the DPIA attachment</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Brief the CISO.</strong> Purview + Entra + Defender is the agentic trust story. Deloitte advises; Microsoft delivers the controls.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>30-minute CISO brief scheduled before Wave 1 build</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Show the trust triad (Purview · Entra · Defender)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Walk audit-row + HITL gate evidence chain</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>CISO sign-off captured in the Wave 1 charter</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · pulled into Wave 1 design (Ch 20) · required at L4 (Ch 22)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch5">Ch 7</a> audit-row schema · <a href="#ch6">Ch 8</a> persona surface · client legal / privacy team</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Sensitivity labels · label → gate matrix · DPIA-ready data-flow diagram · CISO sign-off</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next ref →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch8">Ch 10 · Entra — the Identity Plane</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Note</div>
        Deloitte advises on Purview configuration but never holds client
        keys or labels. Configuration lives in the client tenant.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 8 — ENTRA ===== -->
    <section id="ch8" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 10 · Growth Platform 5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Microsoft Entra — the Identity Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Identity for humans <em>and</em> agents. Conditional access, workload identities, agent identities.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Multiple agents need to act on behalf of multiple personas with audit trails.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>"Which agent did what, for whom, when, under whose authority." Entra answers it.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>L2 onward.</strong> Every Foundry agent gets an Entra workload identity.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Give every agent its own identity.</strong> APEX persona resolver binds Entra workload IDs to agent definitions.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Create Entra workload ID per agent</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>APEX persona resolver wired to Entra binding</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Agent identity catalog maintained in Foundry</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No shared service principal across agents</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire conditional access.</strong> Agents inherit access policy from their persona, not from the operator.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Conditional Access policies authored per persona</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>On-behalf-of (OBO) flow tested end-to-end</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Privileged Identity Management for agent admin roles</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Access review cadence scheduled (quarterly)</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Bind to audit rows.</strong> Every agent action records the Entra identity. Forensics becomes trivial.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Entra OID stamped on every audit row</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Audit-row schema includes agent + operator + persona</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Purview lineage links audit row to identity</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Sample forensic query rehearsed for CISO demo</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Test the off-boarding.</strong> When an agent retires, its identity revokes — APEX adapter handles it.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>APEX adapter wired to Entra revocation API</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Off-boarding workflow tested in GSSC Lab</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Stale-identity sweep scheduled (monthly)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Audit-row trail confirms revocation timestamp</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · pulled into Wave 1 design (Ch 20)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch7">Ch 9</a> labels &amp; gate matrix · client Entra tenant · APEX persona resolver</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Workload IDs per agent · Conditional Access policies · audit-row → identity binding · off-boarding tested</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next ref →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch9">Ch 11 · D365 — the Consumer Plane</a> (L4 only) · or back to <a href="#ch11">Ch 20</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 9 — D365 ===== -->
    <section id="ch9" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 11 · Growth Platform 6</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Dynamics 365 — the Consumer Plane</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>What it is</td><td>Customer Insights, Sales, Service, Commerce — the consumer/customer-facing surface.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Practice is ready for L4. Agents face the end consumer through loyalty, support, commerce.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Practice cares about</td><td>Consumer agentic = largest blast radius. Largest revenue. Largest reference value.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ladder fit</td><td><strong>L4 only.</strong> Do not lead with D365 before B2B is proven.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Confirm L3 is producing ROI.</strong> No L4 without an L3 reference inside the practice.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>L3 CoE has 2+ quarters of running ROI</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Audit-row evidence chain unbroken in production</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Practice leader signs off "ready for consumer"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Reference customer letter on file</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Map consumer journeys.</strong> Loyalty, support, recommendation, returns, dynamic pricing.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Journey workshop with CMO + CXO + CDO</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Score each journey on blast radius × regulatory × ROI</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify highest-trust journey for first agent</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Top 3 candidates locked for L4 charter</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pull the Merch Agentic Client Architecture.</strong> The canonical APEX consumer pancake.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pull pancake from APEX repo (already shipped)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map client data planes to pancake layers</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify consent / identity / returns gaps</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Gap-closure plan with CIO + CDO + CMO</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wire D365 Customer Insights → Foundry agent → Copilot/web surface.</strong> The L4 triad.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>D365 CI instance provisioned in client tenant</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Foundry agent reads CI profile + Fabric RTI signals</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Surface deployed: Copilot Studio + branded web embed</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identity continuity via Entra across the triad</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Hardened HITL.</strong> Consumer-facing = highest gate maturity. Defaults from APEX Core Part 8.3.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Zero auto-decisions to consumer on day one</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>HITL approver staffing model in place 24×7</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Rollback plan and kill-switch tested</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>HITL false-positive rate threshold defined for auto-promotion</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip advisory">Advisory Reference</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Cross-cutting · L4 prerequisite · do not pull before <a href="#ch12">Ch 21</a> ROI is proven</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch12">Ch 21 L3 maturity</a> (gate) · CMO + CXO + CDO triad · Merch Agentic Client Architecture</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">D365 CI ↔ Foundry ↔ Copilot triad wired · consumer channels bound · hardened HITL policy</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch13">Ch 22 · L4 B2C Transformation</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <div class="callout-label">Trap</div>
        Sellers who jump from L1 to L4 lose practice trust. Consumer
        agents need internal-agent muscle memory first. Sequence matters.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== PART IV — FUNCTIONAL AREAS =========== -->
    <section class="part-opener" id="part-fa">
      <div class="part-label">Part IV</div>
      <h1 class="part-title">Functional Areas & Scenario Mapping</h1>
      <p class="part-intro">
        Sellers who walk into a CFO meeting and guess wrong lose the room
        in 90 seconds. Sellers who know the CFO's top three priorities,
        the pain signals behind them, and the APEX scenarios that move
        the number, walk out with a kickoff date. This part is the
        deepest learning section of the handbook — six functional-area
        Cliff Notes, a 30-minute discovery framework, and a master
        scenario-to-service catalog you can hand to any practice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 12 — DISCOVERY FRAMEWORK ===== -->
    <section id="ch-fa-discover" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 12</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Functional Area Discovery — the 30-Minute Framework</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Goal</td><td>In 30 minutes with a functional leader, extract 3 priorities · 3 pain signals · 3 mapped scenarios.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output</td><td>A single index card: <em>priority → pain → scenario → bundle</em>. Feeds the Scenario Matcher.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>When</td><td>After the practice leader opens the door — before the L2 SOW is drafted.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Posture</td><td>You are a student, not a vendor. Ask. Listen. Map afterward.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>The 5-Question Discovery Script</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Open with the metric.</strong> "What's the top number you're held to this year — and how far off baseline are you tracking?"</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Write the metric name + target on the index card</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Capture the gap-vs-baseline figure they admit</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Mark the metric as quarterly · annual · continuous</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Note who else is held to the same number</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Reverse the timeline.</strong> "What would have to be true in 90 days for you to feel ahead?"</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Capture the 90-day "ahead" definition in their words</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>List the 2–3 leading indicators they care about</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm timing aligns with a Wave 1 window</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Note any board / investor commitments in the path</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Surface the constraint.</strong> "What's blocking you from getting there today — capacity, data, decision speed, or risk posture?"</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pick the dominant constraint from their answer</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Drill one level: capacity = headcount? skills? cycles?</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Test a counterfactual: "if X were unlimited, what then?"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map constraint to APEX scenario candidates</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Test the scenario.</strong> "If an agent could handle <em>[name a concrete decision]</em> overnight, would that move your number?"</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Name a concrete decision, not a concept</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Score their reaction: enthusiastic · curious · skeptical</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>If skeptical, swap to a different scenario</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Lock the top scenario on the index card</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Confirm the bundle shape.</strong> "We have a Wave 1 pattern that runs in 90 days for roughly <em>[range]</em>. Should I schedule the kickoff?"</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Quote the bundle by name + range</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm budget owner is in the room (or named)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Propose a kickoff date within 14 days</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Get a written or verbal commitment before leaving</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip ready">Phase 1 · Ready</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 4 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 3 target practice + Tech Leader · per-functional-area context (Ch 13–17)</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Index card filled: priority · pain · scenario · bundle · Microsoft attach</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch-gccs">Ch 4 · Book a GSSC Lab slot</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>The Index Card (fill it during the meeting)</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Slot</th><th>What goes here</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Priority</td><td>The number they're measured on</td><td>"Forecast variance &lt; 5% by Q4"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pain Signal</td><td>The gap they admitted</td><td>"We're at 12% today"</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scenario</td><td>APEX agent that closes the gap</td><td>Forecast-Accuracy Agent (RC)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bundle</td><td>Practice Service Bundle</td><td>Wave 1 — Finance Agentic Pilot, 90 days</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Microsoft Attach</td><td>SKUs the client will license</td><td>Fabric F64 · Foundry · Power BI</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">Key Play</div>
        Sellers who run discovery <em>before</em> opening the Scenario
        Matcher get sharper matches. The Matcher is a tool, not a
        shortcut. Five questions in, you can already predict the top
        scenario it will return.
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Guardrail</div>
        Do not take confidential client metrics out of the room without
        explicit permission. Notes are personal; the index card stays
        with you until the client confirms what you can quote in the
        BVA.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 13 — FINANCE & RISK ===== -->
    <section id="ch-fa-finance" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 13 · Functional Area 1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Finance & Risk — CFO · Controller · CRO · CCO · GC</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Buyers</td><td>CFO, Controller, FP&A leader, CRO, Chief Compliance Officer, General Counsel.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Measured on</td><td>EBITDA · cash · forecast accuracy · audit posture · risk register · attestations.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cycle</td><td>Quarterly for CFO; continuous for Risk & Compliance.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Close is too long, forecast misses are public, or auditors are pressing.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Top 5 Priorities</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Close-cycle compression (days, not weeks).</li>
        <li>Forecast accuracy (variance &lt; benchmark).</li>
        <li>Working-capital optimization (DSO/DPO/inventory).</li>
        <li>Audit readiness and continuous control attestation.</li>
        <li>Cost-to-serve transparency by SKU · customer · channel.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Pain Signals to Listen For</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>"Our close takes 8 days; we want 3."</li>
        <li>"Forecast variance is over 10% — we can't defend that to the board."</li>
        <li>"We can't see daily cash by entity."</li>
        <li>"Auditors are asking for evidence we don't have a clean trail for."</li>
        <li>"We don't truly know cost-to-serve at the customer level."</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Mapped APEX Scenarios</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Edition</th><th>Wave 1 Lever</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Continuous-Close Agent</td><td>Cross-edition</td><td>30–50% close compression</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Forecast-Accuracy Agent</td><td>RC · TH · ER</td><td>Forecast variance reduction</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Working-Capital Agent</td><td>RC · ICE</td><td>DSO/DPO improvement</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Audit-Trail Agent</td><td>All editions</td><td>Continuous control evidence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cost-to-Serve Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Margin visibility per SKU/customer</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        Fabric (data) · Foundry (agents) · Purview (audit labels) · Power
        BI (CFO surface) · Entra (segregation of duties). The CFO buy
        normalizes Fabric capacity for the rest of the practice.
      </div>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Practice Service Bundle</div>
        <strong>Wave 1 — Finance Agentic Pilot</strong> · 90 days ·
        <span class="rev-chip">$1.0–1.8M</span> · Discover → Design → Build → Deploy.
      </div>

      <h3>Discovery Questions (use these in the 30-minute meeting)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>"What's your forecast variance this quarter vs. plan?"</li>
        <li>"Where do your auditors push back hardest right now?"</li>
        <li>"If close took 3 days instead of 8, what would you do with the time?"</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Independence Guardrail</div>
        Finance data is the most sensitive plane in the client.
        Purview labels + HITL gates are non-negotiable before any agent
        touches a journal entry or attestation.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 14 — OPERATIONS & SUPPLY CHAIN ===== -->
    <section id="ch-fa-ops" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 14 · Functional Area 2</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Operations & Supply Chain — COO · CSCO · Plant · Logistics</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Buyers</td><td>COO, CSCO, VP Distribution, VP Logistics, Plant Manager, VP Manufacturing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Measured on</td><td>OEE · fill rate · OTIF · inventory turns · cost-per-unit · safety.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cycle</td><td>Continuous — daily and weekly cadences.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Overstock + stockout coexist · OTIF is below peer · downtime is visible.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Top 5 Priorities</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Demand–supply matching across nodes.</li>
        <li>Inventory optimization (turns, days-on-hand).</li>
        <li>Network / route optimization.</li>
        <li>Asset uptime and integrity.</li>
        <li>Labor scheduling and productivity.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Pain Signals</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>"We're overstocked in DC-East and out-of-stock in DC-West."</li>
        <li>"OTIF is 3 points below benchmark."</li>
        <li>"Trucks run 18% empty by mile."</li>
        <li>"One hour of downtime on Line 3 costs us $X."</li>
        <li>"Labor scheduling is still done in spreadsheets."</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Mapped APEX Scenarios</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Edition</th><th>Wave 1 Lever</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Demand-Forecast Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Forecast accuracy, allocation</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Allocation Agent</td><td>RC</td><td>Cross-node stock balance</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Network-Routing Agent</td><td>RC · ICE</td><td>Empty-mile reduction</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Asset-Integrity Agent</td><td>ER · ICE</td><td>Predictive maintenance windows</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Labor-Schedule Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Coverage vs. cost optimization</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        Fabric Real-Time Intelligence (telemetry) · Foundry · Logic Apps
        (orchestration) · Power BI · IoT/Defender for IoT on the OT side.
      </div>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Practice Service Bundle</div>
        <strong>Wave 1 — Ops Agentic Pilot</strong> · 90 days ·
        <span class="rev-chip">$1.2–2.5M</span> · highest-blast-radius bundle in the catalog.
      </div>

      <h3>Discovery Questions</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>"Where's the gap between forecast and actual hitting you hardest this quarter?"</li>
        <li>"What does an hour of downtime cost on your top asset?"</li>
        <li>"If allocation or routing ran itself overnight, what changes Monday morning?"</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 15 — MARKETING & CX ===== -->
    <section id="ch-fa-mkt" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 15 · Functional Area 3</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Marketing & Customer Experience — CMO · CXO · Brand · Loyalty</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Buyers</td><td>CMO, CXO/CCO, Brand leader, Loyalty leader, Digital VP.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Measured on</td><td>CAC · LTV · NPS · conversion · engagement · retention · service cost-per-contact.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cycle</td><td>Campaign-driven (weeks) · always-on (continuous).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Personalization is stuck at segments, service costs are creeping, attribution is opaque.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Top 5 Priorities</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>1:1 personalization at scale (not segment-based).</li>
        <li>Loyalty conversion and retention lift.</li>
        <li>Channel attribution and media mix.</li>
        <li>Brand-safe content production and review velocity.</li>
        <li>Service-cost deflection (lower-cost customer support).</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Pain Signals</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>"Personalization is still segment-based — we can't go 1:1."</li>
        <li>"We can't attribute revenue across paid · owned · earned."</li>
        <li>"Service costs us $X per contact and rising."</li>
        <li>"Loyalty conversion has been flat for four quarters."</li>
        <li>"Content review is the bottleneck — every campaign waits on legal."</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Mapped APEX Scenarios</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Edition</th><th>Wave 1 Lever</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1:1 Personalization Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Conversion + LTV lift</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Loyalty-Decision Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Tier-upgrade conversion</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Service-Deflection / Triage Agent</td><td>Cross-edition</td><td>Cost-per-contact reduction</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Content-Brand-Safety Agent</td><td>RC · TMT</td><td>Review-cycle compression</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Channel-Attribution Agent</td><td>RC · TH</td><td>Media-mix optimization</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        D365 Customer Insights · Foundry · M365 Copilot · Fabric
        (clickstream) · Purview (consent & PII). This is the L4 platform
        triad — start here when the practice is L3-mature.
      </div>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Practice Service Bundle</div>
        <strong>Wave 1 — CX Agentic Pilot</strong> · often graduates to L4 ·
        <span class="rev-chip">$1.0–2.0M</span> for Wave 1; multi-million in sustain.
      </div>

      <h3>Discovery Questions</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>"What's your top KPI between today and the end of the fiscal year?"</li>
        <li>"Where is CX cost reviewed most aggressively by Finance?"</li>
        <li>"If every service contact could deflect to an agent, what's the goal deflection rate?"</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <div class="callout-label">Trap</div>
        Marketing buyers are early adopters but rarely fund Wave 1 alone.
        Co-sponsor with the CFO ("cost-to-serve") or CIO ("platform
        consolidation") to land the SOW.
      </div>
    </section>

