    <!-- ===== CH 17 — TECH, DATA & TALENT ===== -->
    <section id="ch-fa-tech" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 17 · Functional Area 5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Technology, Data & Talent — CIO · CTO · CDO · CISO · CHRO</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Buyers</td><td>CIO, CTO, CDO, CISO (tech side); CHRO and Chief People Officer (talent side).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Measured on</td><td>TCO · platform consolidation · data quality · time-to-deploy · security posture · time-to-hire · engagement.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cycle</td><td>Annual planning · continuous operate · CISO is event-driven.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sells when</td><td>Agent pilots stuck in PoC · master data is fragmented · CHRO is rebuilding workforce planning.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Top Priorities — Tech side (CIO · CDO · CISO)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Platform consolidation and agent-runtime standardization.</li>
        <li>Data quality, governance, master data.</li>
        <li>Security and Independence-grade controls (Purview · Entra · Defender).</li>
        <li>Time-to-deploy compression for AI workloads.</li>
        <li>App rationalization and TCO reduction.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Top Priorities — Talent side (CHRO)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Recruiting velocity and candidate experience.</li>
        <li>Employee experience and engagement.</li>
        <li>Skill / capability planning against business strategy.</li>
        <li>Internal mobility.</li>
        <li>HR service deflection (lower-cost HR support).</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Pain Signals</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>(CIO) "We have nine agent pilots, zero in production."</li>
        <li>(CDO) "Data is everywhere; truth is nowhere."</li>
        <li>(CISO) "Security review takes weeks per agent — that's the real bottleneck."</li>
        <li>(CHRO) "Time-to-hire is up; we can't see why."</li>
        <li>(CHRO) "Skill-gap data is anecdotal, not modeled."</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Mapped APEX Scenarios</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Buyer</th><th>Wave 1 Lever</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Agent-Platform Standard (APEX-on-Agent-365)</td><td>CIO</td><td>Standardize runtime, kill PoC sprawl</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Master-Data Agent</td><td>CDO</td><td>Single source of truth per domain</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Security-Posture Agent</td><td>CISO</td><td>Continuous Purview/Entra evidence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HR-Service-Desk Agent</td><td>CHRO</td><td>Deflection of Tier-1 HR contacts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Skill-Mapping Agent</td><td>CHRO</td><td>Modeled skill-gap visibility</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout attach">
        <div class="callout-label">Microsoft Attach</div>
        CIO/CDO: Foundry · Fabric · Agent 365. CISO: Purview · Entra ·
        Defender. CHRO: M365 Copilot · Viva · Copilot Studio.
      </div>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Practice Service Bundle</div>
        <strong>Wave 1 — Foundation Agentic Pilot</strong> · CIO is often
        the first internal buyer · <span class="rev-chip">$1.0–2.0M</span> · this bundle unlocks every other functional area's Wave 1.
      </div>

      <h3>Discovery Questions</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>(CIO) "How many agent pilots are running, and how many are in production?"</li>
        <li>(CDO) "What's your single source of truth for customer · product · employee master data?"</li>
        <li>(CHRO) "If HR service-desk deflection rose to 60%, what does your team do instead?"</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">Key Play</div>
        CIO is the unlock buyer for every other functional area. Land
        CIO on APEX-on-Agent-365 first and every subsequent Wave 1 (CFO,
        COO, CMO, CRO) gets faster security review and faster deploy.
      </div>
    </section>

