    <!-- =========== PART V — THE LADDER =========== -->
    <section class="part-opener" id="part3">
      <div class="part-label">Part V</div>
      <h1 class="part-title">The Four-Level Ladder</h1>
      <p class="part-intro">
        Each level is one Cliff Notes chapter: the move, the baby steps,
        the Microsoft platforms that attach, and the single sentence that
        unlocks the next level.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 10 — L1 ===== -->
    <section id="ch10" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 19 · Level 1</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Power BI Dashboard — the Free Gift</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Revenue</td><td><span class="rev-chip">$25–75K</span> · Wedge</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Duration</td><td>5–10 working days end to end.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Buyer</td><td>Practice Tech Leader or LCSP.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Microsoft attach</td><td><span class="ms-chip">Power BI</span> <span class="ms-chip">Fabric (Direct Lake)</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Goal</td><td>Practice <em>sees</em> its pipeline through an APEX lens. Nothing more.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>Seller Steps</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Identify target practice + leader.</strong> RC, TH, HLS, ER, TMT, ICE — pick one.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the practice has 10+ named accounts</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify Industry Leader + Tech Leader + top 3 LCSPs</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Edition status check: RC / TH ship today; others run synthetic</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft account-team intro check — any MCI consumers?</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Request a 30-minute working session.</strong> No slides; discovery only.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Email subject line: "Free Power BI gift for [Practice] portfolio"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Propose 3 time windows</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pre-share the Sellers Dream diagram link only — no deck</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Room with screen-mirroring for live Lab demo</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Pull the practice account list.</strong> Salesforce export, last 8 quarters of bookings.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Data-handling clearance for SF export</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Run the pull: industry · revenue · bookings · status fields</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Mask any client PII (account names → codes if required)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Validate row count against practice expectations</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Score each account against the edition fleet.</strong> RC = 34 agents; map fit per account.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Pull the APEX edition agent catalog</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Score each account 0–3 per agent on fit</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Compute portfolio coverage % per agent</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Identify the top 3 highest-fit accounts</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Build the Power BI page.</strong> Opportunity Heatmap × Microsoft Attach × Wave 1 candidates.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Provision Power BI workspace in the Deloitte tenant</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Wire Direct Lake to the synthetic Fabric model</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Build 3 visuals: heatmap · attach map · candidate list</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Add filter slicers (industry · status · Wave readiness)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Brand check — Deloitte styling, no Microsoft co-brand</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Hand over the .pbix.</strong> They own it. No SOW. No license fee.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Save the .pbix file locally</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Walk through Power BI Desktop with the practice tech contact</span></label></li>
