        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 21 L3 maturity · <a href="#ch9">Ch 11 D365 advisory</a> · <a href="#ch7">Ch 9 Purview consent</a> · Merch Agentic Client Architecture</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Consumer agent in production · Sustain + Managed Services annuity · public case study</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content">Loop · <a href="#ch3">Ch 3 · target the next practice</a> · the case study is the new wedge</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout keyplay">
        <div class="callout-label">The Compounding Effect</div>
        L4 success at Practice A becomes the L1 wedge for Practice B.
        Each practice that climbs to L4 makes the next practice's L1
        conversation shorter, the L2 SOW richer, and the L3 PLC pitch
        irrefutable.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== PART VI — PLAYS =========== -->
    <section class="part-opener" id="part4">
      <div class="part-label">Part VI</div>
      <h1 class="part-title">Plays & Patterns</h1>
      <p class="part-intro">
        The recurring patterns: the 10-minute conversation, the objection
        recoveries, the BVA in 5 bullets. These are the moves you make
        weekly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 14 — 10-MIN PITCH ===== -->
    <section id="ch14" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 23</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The 10-Minute Practice Conversation</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>When</td><td>First time meeting a practice leader.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Outcome</td><td>Agreement to run the L1 Power BI wedge.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tools</td><td>One sheet of paper. The Sellers Dream diagram on your phone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Slot</td><td>10 minutes. No deck. No pitch. Two questions and a gift.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>The Conversation (Minute by Minute)</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minute 1 — Open.</strong> "I lead DMTSP's Consumer Industry team. We accelerate agentic AI delivery on Microsoft. Two questions, then a gift."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Memorize the opening sentence verbatim</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Stay seated · no laptop · pen + paper visible</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Set the contract: "two questions, then a gift"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No DMTSP overview slides — words only</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minutes 2–3 — Q1.</strong> "Which 3 accounts in your portfolio are asking about agentic AI?" Listen. Take notes by hand.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Capture account names verbatim</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Note the buyer name per account, if mentioned</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Probe "asking how?" — capacity · platform · methodology</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Do not pitch — keep the pen moving</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minutes 4–5 — Q2.</strong> "What's blocking you from saying yes faster — capacity, methodology, or Microsoft platform fluency?" Whichever they say, that's your wedge.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Capture the blocker verbatim</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Map blocker → the right wedge (L1 dashboard · Lab demo · BVA)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Probe: "and what does fast look like?"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm the blocker is theirs, not their accounts'</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minutes 6–8 — Show the diagram.</strong> Sellers Dream on your phone. Walk L1 → L4. Land on L1: "Today I'm only here to talk about this box."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Open the Sellers Dream diagram on phone / tablet</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Walk L1 → L4 in under 90 seconds</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Anchor on L1: "this is today's conversation"</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Acknowledge L2–L4 exist; resist scope creep in the moment</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minute 9 — The gift.</strong> "We'll build you a Power BI Opportunity Heatmap for your portfolio. Five days. Free. You own the .pbix."</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Promise: 5 working days · free · they own the .pbix</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>State what you need: account list + 30 min for the data pull</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>No strings: no SOW conversation today</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Confirm Deloitte covers the build cost (internal accelerator budget)</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Minute 10 — Close.</strong> "Who on your team should I work with for the data pull?" Get a name. Schedule the kickoff before you leave.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Get a named contact for the data pull</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Lock kickoff date in the leader's calendar live</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Send confirmation email within 2 hours</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Log the meeting outcome in CRM / opportunity tracker</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip meet">Phase 2 · Meet</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 7 of 12 · Seller Journey</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 1–3 language · Ch 12 discovery script · Ch 4–5 Lab readiness · Sellers Dream on phone</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Practice leader committed to the L1 wedge · data-pull contact named · kickoff scheduled</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content"><a href="#ch10">Ch 19 · L1 Power BI Dashboard</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Why It Works</div>
        Practice leaders are asked for things, not given things. A
        no-strings dashboard reverses the polarity. The leader spends the
        rest of the week looking for a reason to thank you.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 15 — OBJECTIONS ===== -->
    <section id="ch15" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 24</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Objections & Recoveries</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>Top 6 objections</td><td>Same six come up every week. Memorize the recoveries.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Recovery shape</td><td>Acknowledge → Reframe → Offer a smaller next step.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Never</td><td>Argue. Promise Microsoft credits. Discount the SOW to win the deal.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="md-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Objection</th><th>Recovery</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>"We already have an agentic strategy."</td><td>"Great. Then the Power BI dashboard will validate it for free. If it confirms your plan, you've lost nothing."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>"My LCSPs won't sell agentic — they sell their accounts."</td><td>"That's exactly why I bring them a portfolio heatmap, not a methodology. They sell accounts; we sell <em>through</em> accounts."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>"Microsoft's account team is already pitching this."</td><td>"Microsoft sells platform; we sell delivery. Different SKU, different buyer. Two contracts."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>"What's the APEX license cost?"</td><td>"APEX is Deloitte's internal accelerator — there's no license. You pay for our services SOW; APEX is how we deliver faster."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>"Can you bundle the Microsoft credits into your SOW?"</td><td>"No — Independence requires separation. Microsoft co-fund is a parallel motion the Microsoft seller runs. I can introduce you."</td></tr>
          <tr><td>"We don't have Fabric yet."</td><td>"Then L1 is the right starting point. The Power BI dashboard runs on a Fabric trial and proves the case before any capacity buy."</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== CH 16 — BVA ===== -->
    <section id="ch16" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 25</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">BVA in 5 Bullets</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="glance">
        <div class="glance-label">At a Glance</div>
        <table>
          <tr><td>BVA</td><td>Business Value Assessment. Deloitte's structured ROI exercise.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>When</td><td>Before the L2 SOW. Not after. Never as an afterthought.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Output</td><td>Excel model + 1-page summary. Client signs the summary.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Source</td><td><code>references/bva-framework.md</code> in the deloitte-microsoft-docs skill.</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>The Five Bullets That Win the BVA</h3>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Today's cost.</strong> What does the client spend on the decision the agent will make — labor, opportunity cost, error rate?</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Labor cost · FTEs × loaded rate × hours per decision</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Opportunity cost · decisions delayed or skipped</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Error cost · rework + downstream impact + remediation</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Client validates each line item before model is signed</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Tomorrow's cost.</strong> Same line items, with agent + Deloitte services + Microsoft platform consumption modeled.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Residual labor model after agent deployment</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Deloitte services line (Wave 1 + Sustain)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Microsoft consumption line (Fabric · Foundry · Copilot)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Show two contracts separately — never combined</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Velocity delta.</strong> Decisions per week before vs. after. Often the largest line item.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Decisions-per-week baseline measured from current systems</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Target velocity from APEX reference deployments</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>$ value per additional decision quantified</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Conservative velocity range used (low / mid / high)</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Error reduction.</strong> Agent + HITL gate vs. status quo. Audit-row evidence from APEX deployments.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Status-quo error rate captured from client systems</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>APEX reference error rate cited with audit-row backing</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>$ value of avoided errors modeled</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>HITL gate prevents the worst-case error class</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
        <li><details>
          <summary><strong>Wave 1 ROI in dollars.</strong> One number on the summary page. Signed by the client.</summary>
          <div class="subtasks">
            <div class="subtasks-label">Sub-tasks</div>
            <ul>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Single dollar figure on the summary page</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Realistic ROI range: 2–3× in Wave 1, 8–12× across Waves 1–3</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Client signs the summary page (not just the model)</span></label></li>
              <li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>BVA filed with the SOW as exhibit</span></label></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="carry-forward">
        <div class="cf-header">
          <span class="phase-chip sell">Phase 4 · Sell</span>
          <span class="cf-progress">Step 10 of 12 · Seller Journey · (executes inside Ch 20)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-grid">
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">← Inputs</div><div class="cf-content">Ch 12 discovery card · Ch 20 Wave 1 scope · APEX reference deployment numbers</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">→ Produces</div><div class="cf-content">Signed BVA · single Wave 1 ROI dollar figure · SOW exhibit · 2–3× Wave 1, 8–12× Waves 1–3</div></div>
          <div class="cf-cell"><div class="cf-label">Next →</div><div class="cf-content">Returns to <a href="#ch11">Ch 20 · Deploy with APEX accelerators</a></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout warning">
        <div class="callout-label">Trap</div>
        BVAs that promise &gt;5× ROI in Wave 1 lose credibility. APEX
        deployments typically return 2–3× in Wave 1 and 8–12× over Waves
        1–3 combined. Use the realistic curve.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== APPENDIX A =========== -->
    <section id="appA" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Appendix A</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Edition × Practice Map</h1>
      </div>

      <p>Which APEX edition serves which Deloitte practice. Active editions
      can run L1 → L4 today. Planned editions can run L1 with synthetic
      data; L2 needs the edition to be commissioned first.</p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
