    <!-- =========== APPENDIX B =========== -->
    <section id="appB" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Appendix B</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Independence Cheat Sheet</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">The One Test</div>
        Would the SEC/PCAOB conclude Deloitte and Microsoft have a
        commingled commercial offering? Answer must always be <strong>no</strong>.
      </div>

      <h3>Language</h3>
      <div class="saynot">
        <div class="col say">
          <h4>✓ Use</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Deloitte's Microsoft practice (DMTSP)</li>
            <li>Microsoft platform expertise</li>
            <li>Microsoft technology solutions</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col nope">
          <h4>✗ Never Use</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Partner / partnership</li>
            <li>Alliance / strategic alliance</li>
            <li>Joint venture</li>
            <li>Co-sell as a single offering</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Commercial Structure</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Platform licensing: <strong>Client ↔ Microsoft</strong> (always direct).</li>
        <li>Services: <strong>Client ↔ Deloitte</strong> (always separate SOW).</li>
        <li>Microsoft co-fund: parallel motion, never inside the Deloitte SOW.</li>
        <li>APEX: Deloitte internal IP — never licensed, sold, or branded to the client.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Data Plane</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Client data stays in client tenant. Always.</li>
        <li>Deloitte deploys agents <em>onto</em> client tenant; we do not host.</li>
        <li>At engagement exit: client owns agents, data, platform. Deloitte retains framework methodology.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- =========== APPENDIX C =========== -->
    <section id="appC" class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Appendix C</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">One-Page Practice Pitch Template</h1>
      </div>

      <p>Print this. Take it to the practice leader. Fill it in live during
      the 10-minute conversation. Leave it with them.</p>

      <div class="callout note">
        <div class="callout-label">Template</div>
        <p><strong>For:</strong> _______________________________ Practice (RC · TH · HLS · ER · TMT · ICE)</p>
        <p><strong>Leader:</strong> ____________________ &nbsp; <strong>Date:</strong> __________</p>
        <p><strong>Three accounts asking about agentic AI today:</strong></p>
        <ol>
          <li>____________________________________________________</li>
          <li>____________________________________________________</li>
          <li>____________________________________________________</li>
        </ol>
        <p><strong>Top blocker (circle one):</strong> &nbsp; capacity · methodology · Microsoft fluency · funding · other ______</p>
        <p><strong>L1 wedge offer:</strong> Power BI Opportunity Heatmap, 5 working days, free, you own the .pbix.</p>
        <p><strong>Practice contact for data pull:</strong> ____________________________________________________</p>
        <p><strong>Kickoff scheduled:</strong> __________ &nbsp; <strong>Delivery date:</strong> __________</p>
        <p><strong>L2 unlock sentence (to use at handover):</strong> <em>"Now you can see every place APEX would compress your delivery — want to act on the top three?"</em></p>
      </div>

      <div class="callout independence">
        <div class="callout-label">Final Reminder</div>
        Deloitte sells <strong>Agentic AI Delivery Services</strong> on the
        client's Microsoft platform. APEX is how we deliver fast. Two
        contracts. Always.
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
